extraction_notes: |
  - Read from Dragons and Gods printed 38-40 (the species entry), 17 (the Dragon Experience Table) and 50 (Hatchling Dragon as an optional Player Character), each number read off a page render because the text layer carries the digit cipher (206+ 1 2 for 2D6+12, 404x l O for 4D4x10).
  - SHAPE COPIED FROM chiang-ku-dragon: a hatchling variant and an adult variant carrying attribute dice, pools, horror factor and bonuses; everything else shared. The top-level skills, magic and psionics describe the HATCHLING, because printed 50 makes the hatchling the player character and a variant cannot override `magic` or `psionics`. The adult''s psionics and magic are recorded as special abilities.
  - xp_table is the shared Dragon Experience Table, printed 17: the lower bound of each of levels 1-15. Printed 50 says to use it for a hatchling player character.
  - starting_money 0 and no equipment: printed 50, "start with no possessions".
  - "+N on all other saving throws" is written out as fourteen save keys, the gargoyle-lord convention: every save the sheet draws except horror_factor (stated separately) and coma_death_pct (a percentage).
  - Unlike the other species, the Night Stalker''s hatchling starts its language AND math skills at 98%, so advanced math is 98% for both variants and no skill override is needed. All other skills start at first level proficiency (catalog base plus the printed bonus). No category bonus is printed for the selections.
  - "Literate in Dragonese/Elven 98% and two other languages ... plus speaks four ADDITIONAL languages" is read as six spoken languages (the two it reads plus four) and three literacies. Language: Dragonese is granted because the page names the literacy and the four spoken languages are called additional.
  - Scholar is the catalog''s Technical category. "Include I.Q. bonus" is not printed for this species.
  - The hatchling knows every wizard spell of levels one and two outright, and gains 1D4 from levels 3-4 at each even level to 14. The first is a list the catalog does not name and the second is dice-valued, so the magic block states the level gate and no count; both are in special_abilities.
  - The printed bio-regeneration is 6D6 S.D.C. per melee round, "4D6 per minute for hatchlings", transcribed as printed.
  - Rifts conversion block (printed 40) omitted, as chiang-ku omits its own.
  - Average adult level (2D4+5), habitat, life span, enemies and allies are lore, recorded below.
