## Lore

Night Stalkers are held to be the tricksters and villains of dragonkind, emblems of darkness and the undead. They are nocturnal, ally with vampires and other night predators, and like to use animated dead, mummies and zombies. Many are masters of thieves, assassins and deception, with a deep, soft, persuasive voice that has talked many humans and monsters to their doom. Many hunt, torment and eat humanoids, and when they are not hunting they are stirring up bloodshed and turmoil.

By day they keep to an underground lair; bright light nearly blinds them, although otherwise they function as well by day as by night. They are dull green, blue-green, blue-black, dark grey or black, with a long serpentine body, large slender black wings, spikes along the spine, a reptilian head with watery blue eyes, webbed horns on the cheeks and chin whiskers. They covet gems, precious works of art, magic and power more than most dragons, and most are thoroughly evil.

**Alignment:** Any, but typically anarchist (33%) or evil (60%).

**Size:** 8 to 10 feet tall, 30 to 40 feet long, with a 60 foot (18.3 m) wingspan.

**Weight:** 2.5 tons.

**Habitat:** Anywhere, but usually skulking around the domains of humans, Elves, Dwarves, Kobolds, Ogres and Wolfen. They love big cities, and especially the Western Empire, the Old Kingdom and the Land of the South Winds.

**Average Life Span:** 4000-6000 years; some reach 8000.

**Enemies:** Every walk of life, mortal and supernatural. Knights, palladins, good priests and Champions of Light in particular.

**Allies:** Vampires above all; also evil sorcerers, witches, priests of darkness, demons, deevils, dark gods and anyone who serves their plans.

## GM Notes

A Night Stalker hatchling is the obvious villain''s child: a schemer with good espionage and rogue picks, every first and second level wizard spell, and a black-flame breath that lacks the adult''s corrupting enchantment. Its greed and hunger for control are the hooks, and its poor day vision is a real handicap for a party that travels by daylight.
